00:21:46,124 --> 00:21:48,908
- Yeah and a vacant lot.

507
00:21:48,908 --> 00:21:51,043
- OK, now, cut that out.

508
00:21:51,043 --> 00:21:53,363
- [Voiceover] Without
question, this was the capsule

509
00:21:53,363 --> 00:21:56,243
that had put Douglas into orbit.

510
00:21:56,243 --> 00:21:58,154
Without question, Douglas was
(laughter)

511
00:21:58,154 --> 00:21:59,674
gone, without a trace.

512
00:21:59,674 --> 00:22:01,638
- Douglas was pear shaped,
very short, and stood the

513
00:22:01,638 --> 00:22:02,471
whole way.

514
00:22:05,727 --> 00:22:09,394
- Ray, look, it's filled
with Schlit's cans.

515
00:22:10,252 --> 00:22:12,398
- Oh, thank goodness Les
Paul is backing them up

516
00:22:12,398 --> 00:22:13,231
on guitar.

517
00:22:16,354 --> 00:22:19,021
- Earl, it's not your break yet.

518
00:22:19,874 --> 00:22:22,130
- The helicopter pilot who
had discovered the capsule

519
00:22:22,130 --> 00:22:25,757
was dead, horribly mangled
in a way no one had ever

520
00:22:25,757 --> 00:22:27,721
seen before.
- [Tom] Oh, quit playing with

521
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:29,054
his face, Aaron.

522
00:22:30,834 --> 00:22:31,925
(doorbell ringing)
- [Crow] Meanwhile,

523
00:22:31,925 --> 00:22:34,425
in a soap opera, not far away.

524
00:22:37,436 --> 00:22:39,478
- What do you want?

525
00:22:39,478 --> 00:22:41,282
- Oh, Laura, how are you?

526
00:22:41,282 --> 00:22:42,475
- How's Jimmy?

527
00:22:42,475 --> 00:22:45,132
- Oh, he's fine, I just sent
him over to Mrs. Williams.

528
00:22:45,132 --> 00:22:46,049
- Air kiss.

529
00:22:49,966 --> 00:22:51,130
- Have some coffee?

530
00:22:51,130 --> 00:22:52,520
- No, no thanks.

531
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:54,245
- Yes, please.

532
00:22:54,245 --> 00:22:56,328
- Make it good this time.

533
00:22:57,762 --> 00:23:00,610
- Usually keeps a bunch
of M and Ms in that bowl.

534
00:23:00,610 --> 00:23:04,247
- Oh, feel free to stink
the house up, geez.

535
00:23:04,247 --> 00:23:08,126
- Well, here's the witch's
brew, I mean coffee.

536
00:23:08,126 --> 00:23:13,117
♫ Times like these were
made for Taster's Joy ♫

537
00:23:13,117 --> 00:23:16,555
- It's about Frank, isn't it?
(spitting)

538
00:23:16,555 --> 00:23:18,556
- Ruth, the capsule came back.

539
00:23:18,556 --> 00:23:20,635
- This coffee's warmer than Frank is.

540
00:23:20,635 --> 00:23:22,046
- What about Frank?

541
00:23:22,046 --> 00:23:24,438
- I don't know, he had all
the emergency equipment

542
00:23:24,438 --> 00:23:25,966
he needed, but--

543
00:23:25,966 --> 00:23:27,718
- He was just stupid.

544
00:23:27,718 --> 00:23:28,887
- Well.

545
00:23:28,887 --> 00:23:30,761
- What is it all about?

546
00:23:30,761 --> 00:23:33,719
- Shot was a success, the
capsule did come back--

547
00:23:33,719 --> 00:23:35,567
- But Frank didn't.

548
00:23:35,567 --> 00:23:37,043
- It's just that we don't know whether the

549
00:23:37,043 --> 00:23:38,883
radiation repellent worked or not.

550
00:23:38,883 --> 00:23:40,731
- Oh, I know I shouldn't feel this way.

551
00:23:40,731 --> 00:23:44,891
It's his life, but, well,
ever since Harry died,

552
00:23:44,891 --> 00:23:46,919
Frank's been like a father to Jimmy.

553
00:23:46,919 --> 00:23:48,651
- Harry, wait, slow down.

554
00:23:48,651 --> 00:23:50,964
- Try not to even think
about it right now.

555
00:23:50,964 --> 00:23:52,287
- What am I going to tell Jimmy?

556
00:23:52,287 --> 00:23:53,287
- Who's Jimmy?

557
00:23:53,287 --> 00:23:55,038
- Would you like me to spend the night?

558
00:23:55,038 --> 00:23:57,966
- Oh, you'd like that, wouldn't you?

559
00:23:57,966 --> 00:23:59,530
- I've got to get back to the lab now.

560
00:23:59,530 --> 00:24:01,130
- I don't want to spend
anymore time with this

561
00:24:01,130 --> 00:24:02,130
than I already have.

562
00:24:02,130 --> 00:24:03,130
- There's anything I can do.

563
00:24:03,130 --> 00:24:04,130
- Thank you, Carl.

564
00:24:04,130 --> 00:24:05,516
- Of course we'll be
cutting off the pension,

565
00:24:05,516 --> 00:24:06,766
you understand.

566
00:24:09,598 --> 00:24:10,599
- Hi, Dr. Carl.

567
00:24:10,599 --> 00:24:11,772
- Hi, ya space cadet.
- [Crow] Frank's dead.

568
00:24:11,772 --> 00:24:14,199
- I thought you were
over at Mrs. Williams.

569
00:24:14,199 --> 00:24:17,277
- I had to get some more rocket parts.

570
00:24:17,277 --> 00:24:19,161
When's Uncle Frank coming home?

571
00:24:19,161 --> 00:24:21,614
- You'll have to make due
with Uncle Bob and Uncle Jim

572
00:24:21,614 --> 00:24:25,160
and Uncle Phil and
Uncle Roy and Uncle Tim.

573
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:26,527
- Burned on reentry, huh?

574
00:24:26,527 --> 00:24:27,931
- --take me fishing.
- [Carl] Well, some trips

575
00:24:27,931 --> 00:24:29,362
are longer than we expected.

576
00:24:29,362 --> 00:24:30,650
- Make other plans, Jimmy.

577
00:24:30,650 --> 00:24:32,279
- What's wrong with Mommy?

578
00:24:32,279 --> 00:24:34,038
- Mommy's not feeling very well.

579
00:24:34,038 --> 00:24:35,596
But suppose you went upstairs
and when we're all through,

580
00:24:35,596 --> 00:24:37,406
we'll have a nice big ice cream soda, huh?

581
00:24:37,406 --> 00:24:39,823
- Now that solves everything.

582
00:24:41,202 --> 00:24:43,131
- Hey, Timmy, my dad's dead
again, can I come over for

583
00:24:43,131 --> 00:24:44,477
dinner?

584
00:24:44,477 --> 00:24:45,888
- Laura, I can't take anymore.

585
00:24:45,888 --> 00:24:47,691
- Oh, look, let's not make
a bigger deal out of this

586
00:24:47,691 --> 00:24:50,955
than it really is.
(phone ringing, yelling)

587
00:24:50,955 --> 00:24:51,788
- Sheesh.

588
00:24:53,493 --> 00:24:56,651
What's that, face like
spinach dip? Horribly mangled?

589
00:24:56,651 --> 00:24:59,203
No dental records? Too bad.

590
00:24:59,203 --> 00:25:01,487
- All right, I'll be right over.

591
00:25:01,487 --> 00:25:04,003
- Well, looks like he
died in a state of sin.

592
00:25:04,003 --> 00:25:06,038
- They've located the camper.

593
00:25:06,038 --> 00:25:08,155
- Two word, closed casket.

594
00:25:08,155 --> 00:25:12,038
- I'll let you know as soon as I find out.

595
00:25:12,038 --> 00:25:14,767
- Wait, Carl, I want to go with you.

596
00:25:14,767 --> 00:25:17,727
- Honey, he'll call if there's any news.

597
00:25:17,727 --> 00:25:19,996
- No, I want to be with you.

598
00:25:19,996 --> 00:25:22,163
(humming)

599
00:25:28,315 --> 00:25:30,648
(whooshing)

600
00:25:38,571 --> 00:25:40,738
(humming)

601
00:25:44,803 --> 00:25:46,484
- Hey.
- [Crow] Hi.

602
00:25:46,484 --> 00:25:48,651
(humming)

603
00:25:56,207 --> 00:25:58,483
- Hello.
- [Crow] Yes?

604
00:25:58,483 --> 00:26:01,239
- I don't get you.
- [Crow] Oh.

605
00:26:01,239 --> 00:26:03,443
- Are you mad?
- [Crow] No, no.

606
00:26:03,443 --> 00:26:06,207
- Good, because I want
to like you, but I just

607
00:26:06,207 --> 00:26:08,637
don't understand where you're coming from.

608
00:26:08,637 --> 00:26:11,763
- Sure, what's not to get though, Gypsy?

609
00:26:11,763 --> 00:26:13,515
I just am, I hang out.

610
00:26:13,515 --> 00:26:17,043
- Oh, oh, I know, it's
just that, you know,

611
00:26:17,043 --> 00:26:21,087
I don't really get you.
- [Crow] Yeah, OK.

612
00:26:21,087 --> 00:26:23,035
Maybe I can help.

613
00:26:23,035 --> 00:26:26,687
To start with, I'm a
robot, I use cyber based

614
00:26:26,687 --> 00:26:29,561
bubble memory, is that
what's confusing you?

615
00:26:29,561 --> 00:26:32,077
- No.
- [Crow] Is it that I work

616
00:26:32,077 --> 00:26:35,402
off Unix and can use a
variety of operating systems?

617
00:26:35,402 --> 00:26:37,843
- Well, I guess that's a start.

618
00:26:37,843 --> 00:26:41,371
- Well, I've undergone a
complex personal evolution

619
00:26:41,371 --> 00:26:43,917
wherein painful confusion
has given way to what I like

620
00:26:43,917 --> 00:26:46,076
to think of as some degree
of wisdom, culminating

621
00:26:46,076 --> 00:26:48,956
in my current Zarathustrian sense of self,

622
00:26:48,956 --> 00:26:50,046
is that it?

623
00:26:50,046 --> 00:26:51,046
- No.

624
00:26:51,046 --> 00:26:53,516
If that helps you it's good, but--

625
00:26:53,516 --> 00:26:56,687
- Gypsy, I don't know
what, is it that I often

626
00:26:56,687 --> 00:26:57,930
panic while making sandwiches?

627
00:26:57,930 --> 00:27:01,197
- Yeah, well, well, maybe
it's that kind of thing.

628
00:27:01,197 --> 00:27:03,276
- Is it that I smell
conspiracy in everything and I

629
00:27:03,276 --> 00:27:06,047
don't know what I mean most of the time?

630
00:27:06,047 --> 00:27:08,971
- Well, that's perhaps a
small piece of the puzzle,

631
00:27:08,971 --> 00:27:09,804
but I...

632
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:13,087
- Gypsy, is it an odor?

633
00:27:13,087 --> 00:27:14,337
- No, well, no.

634
00:27:15,967 --> 00:27:18,360
Well, maybe it's Tom I don't get.

635
00:27:18,360 --> 00:27:21,485
- Oh, brother, like a Zippo
lighter without any flint,

636
00:27:21,485 --> 00:27:22,818
I can't believe.

637
00:27:25,997 --> 00:27:27,770
(humming)

638
00:27:27,770 --> 00:27:29,878
- Tom?
- [Tom] Yo.

639
00:27:29,878 --> 00:27:31,638
- I don't get you.

640
00:27:31,638 --> 00:27:33,690
- Nobody does, I'm the wind, baby.

641
00:27:33,690 --> 00:27:35,857
(humming)

642
00:27:37,799 --> 00:27:40,216
(calm music)

643
00:27:45,247 --> 00:27:47,650
(humming)

644
00:27:47,650 --> 00:27:49,131
- Geez, aren't there
any roads in this town?

645
00:27:49,131 --> 00:27:50,919
- It's a hover Bonneville.

646
00:27:50,919 --> 00:27:52,971
- I think this is the movie
version of Darkness Visible

647
00:27:52,971 --> 00:27:54,471
by William Stylen.

648
00:27:55,523 --> 00:27:57,078
- Wait, I want to come with you.

649
00:27:57,078 --> 00:27:58,485
- No, Ruth, you stay here.

650
00:27:58,485 --> 00:28:00,975
- Geez, you're high maintenance.

651
00:28:00,975 --> 00:28:05,484
- Well, could I have the keys
so I can listen to the radio?

652
00:28:05,484 --> 00:28:06,317
- Yes.

653
00:28:08,365 --> 00:28:10,926
- No, Jim Taylor, the helicopter pilot.

654
00:28:10,926 --> 00:28:12,008
- How did it happen?

655
00:28:12,008 --> 00:28:14,621
- We don't know, sir, we
were having contact with it

656
00:28:14,621 --> 00:28:16,372
from the ground car.

657
00:28:16,372 --> 00:28:19,048
Suddenly, he let out a
yell, and then went blind.

658
00:28:19,048 --> 00:28:20,606
There was nothing we could do.

659
00:28:20,606 --> 00:28:23,121
- You better take a
look at the body, Carl.

660
00:28:23,121 --> 00:28:24,924
- He said garp, then he
said good, and then he died.

661
00:28:24,924 --> 00:28:26,525
- I've never seen anything like it.

662
00:28:26,525 --> 00:28:28,140
He shriveled up like a dried prune.

663
00:28:28,140 --> 00:28:29,450
- Like a drag queen?

664
00:28:29,450 --> 00:28:32,125
- Looks like some kind of
a burn, but it didn't touch

665
00:28:32,125 --> 00:28:33,644
his hair or his clothes.

666
00:28:33,644 --> 00:28:35,607
- But he's horribly mutilated.

667
00:28:35,607 --> 00:28:37,899
- That's what's left of him.

668
00:28:37,899 --> 00:28:41,056
- They shaved his mustache, those animals.

669
00:28:41,056 --> 00:28:44,723
- There's something
else I want to show you.

670
00:28:47,020 --> 00:28:49,048
- Rick, could I get a ride home?

671
00:28:49,048 --> 00:28:50,366
- What do you make of this, Carl?

672
00:28:50,366 --> 00:28:52,460
- Looks like a meadow muffin.

673
00:28:52,460 --> 00:28:54,772
- They look like severe burns.

674
00:28:54,772 --> 00:28:56,290
- What could have caused such burns?

675
00:28:56,290 --> 00:28:57,899
- Mexican food?

676
00:28:57,899 --> 00:28:59,813
- I don't know.

677
00:28:59,813 --> 00:29:02,059
Probably some kid's prank.

678
00:29:02,059 --> 00:29:04,931
- Yeah, kids are always mutilating people.

679
00:29:04,931 --> 00:29:07,580
- Oh, good, now what about the capsule?

680
00:29:07,580 --> 00:29:09,123
- The equipment's on the way now.

681
00:29:09,123 --> 00:29:11,927
- All right, but I want you
to stay here until it arrives.

682
00:29:11,927 --> 00:29:14,045
I don't want anything
disturbed until Dr. Logan

683
00:29:14,045 --> 00:29:15,741
has had a chance to examine it carefully.

684
00:29:15,741 --> 00:29:17,408
- All right, doctor.

685
00:29:18,896 --> 00:29:20,816
- We'd better get back to
the lab, there's nothing

686
00:29:20,816 --> 00:29:22,460
more we can do here.

687
00:29:22,460 --> 00:29:25,572
- Robert Goule and Martin
Milner, they're cops.

688
00:29:25,572 --> 00:29:27,892
- What are we gonna tell Ruth?

689
00:29:27,892 --> 00:29:29,406
- What do you mean, we?

690
00:29:29,406 --> 00:29:31,260
- Can we, Carl?

691
00:29:31,260 --> 00:29:32,808
- What do you mean?

692
00:29:32,808 --> 00:29:35,419
- There's no real proof
that Douglas is dead.

693
00:29:35,419 --> 00:29:36,487
There's no body.

694
00:29:36,487 --> 00:29:37,579
- No bounce.

695
00:29:37,579 --> 00:29:39,331
- Maybe we shouldn't tell her anything.

696
00:29:39,331 --> 00:29:41,013
- Yeah, let's toy with her for a while.

697
00:29:41,013 --> 00:29:43,288
- Nobody hopes for a
miracle more than I, Henry.

698
00:29:43,288 --> 00:29:44,291
- Pope does.

699
00:29:44,291 --> 00:29:47,005
- But there's no sense grabbing at straws.

700
00:29:47,005 --> 00:29:49,172
Even assuming he was blown
clear of the wreckage before

701
00:29:49,172 --> 00:29:51,732
the doctors had ran out.

702
00:29:51,732 --> 00:29:52,968
- You're deep, Terry.

703
00:29:52,968 --> 00:29:54,940
- The wreckage here is
enough to tell the story.

704
00:29:54,940 --> 00:29:56,336
- I'm not convinced.

705
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:59,282
The condition of that body.

706
00:29:59,282 --> 00:30:01,476
Something's not right.

707
00:30:01,476 --> 00:30:03,814
- We'll probably get the
facts in the laboratory.

708
00:30:03,814 --> 00:30:05,133
- Maybe you're right.

709
00:30:05,133 --> 00:30:05,966
- Hungry?

710
00:30:08,537 --> 00:30:11,686
- Couldn't even afford
to hang the chalkboard.

711
00:30:11,686 --> 00:30:14,186
- Still mad, Evan? Let's talk.

712
00:30:15,046 --> 00:30:16,770
- I thought you went home.

713
00:30:16,770 --> 00:30:17,962
- Too much on my mind.

714
00:30:17,962 --> 00:30:20,122
- You've got a bit of
toilet paper on your shoe.

715
00:30:20,122 --> 00:30:22,538
- I've never been home, either.

716
00:30:22,538 --> 00:30:24,734
Kept thinking about the body.

717
00:30:24,734 --> 00:30:26,379
I've never seen anything like it.

718
00:30:26,379 --> 00:30:29,044
Sure I've been, I'm
trying to find an answer.

719
00:30:29,044 --> 00:30:30,604
- Trying to find a microphone.

720
00:30:30,604 --> 00:30:31,934
- Here I am.
- [Carl] Did you come up

721
00:30:31,934 --> 00:30:32,938
with anything?

722
00:30:32,938 --> 00:30:36,219
- Look, you know enough
about these things.

723
00:30:36,219 --> 00:30:38,546
- Hey, that's my wife.

724
00:30:38,546 --> 00:30:39,730
- This is human tissue.

725
00:30:39,730 --> 00:30:41,264
- Correct.

726
00:30:41,264 --> 00:30:43,214
- But it's different, though.

727
00:30:43,214 --> 00:30:45,171
Never seen anything quite like it.

728
00:30:45,171 --> 00:30:46,731
- I took from Taylor's body.

729
00:30:46,731 --> 00:30:49,665
He was literally cooked to
death in a matter of seconds.

730
00:30:49,665 --> 00:30:51,237
- That sounds delicious.

731
00:30:51,237 --> 00:30:54,130
- Something so charged
with radiated energy...

732
00:30:54,130 --> 00:30:55,786
(mumbles)

733
00:30:55,786 --> 00:30:57,409
- You in front of the
capsule came back with

734
00:30:57,409 --> 00:30:58,704
radioactive energy?

735
00:30:58,704 --> 00:31:00,733
- The capsule didn't kill Taylor.

736
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:02,129
Here.

737
00:31:02,129 --> 00:31:06,449
- Look, could we get a
miracle here or something?

738
00:31:06,449 --> 00:31:08,696
- Tiny scraps of metal.

739
00:31:08,696 --> 00:31:09,697
Seems normal.

740
00:31:09,697 --> 00:31:11,864
- It is, no radioactivity.

741
00:31:12,786 --> 00:31:14,973
- I don't like you.
- [Carl] --something else.

742
00:31:14,973 --> 00:31:17,657
- Remember the scorch mark
on the ground near the body?

743
00:31:17,657 --> 00:31:18,851
- Yeah, that was fine.

744
00:31:18,851 --> 00:31:20,618
- [Henry] --kill Taylor
stood, or was placed

745
00:31:20,618 --> 00:31:22,901
right where the body was.

746
00:31:22,901 --> 00:31:25,009
Analysis from the grass from that spot,

747
00:31:25,009 --> 00:31:27,613
showed clearly the same
effects upon Taylor's body.

748
00:31:27,613 --> 00:31:29,620
- Henry, I know what
you're driving at, but--

749
00:31:29,620 --> 00:31:31,649
- Shut up.
- [Carl] --but it's

750
00:31:31,649 --> 00:31:32,650
impossible.

751
00:31:32,650 --> 00:31:34,241
Douglas couldn't have survived.

752
00:31:34,241 --> 00:31:35,576
- [Henry] Why not?

753
00:31:35,576 --> 00:31:37,570
The nosecone of the capsule did.

754
00:31:37,570 --> 00:31:38,438
The chute opened.

755
00:31:38,438 --> 00:31:39,884
- I'm aware of that.

756
00:31:39,884 --> 00:31:41,551
(mumbles)

757
00:31:41,551 --> 00:31:43,107
Pass over our radio signal.

758
00:31:43,107 --> 00:31:44,663
- Passover gradient?

759
00:31:44,663 --> 00:31:46,830
(mumbles)

